**Definition 2.4 (complete raw carrier).** Use ARC Definition 6.2's physical
codec with 74 port lists, actual eight-track cells, creation positions,
heads, latches, PC, ownership/tokens and finite control slots of this
graph. Retain raw partially written control stores separately from the
last complete active table. Until DONE the actual bootstrap stays active.
After raw DONE, a unique well-typed decoded row has its actual primitive
successor when enabled; absent/duplicate/out-of-range fields give no main
edge. Earlier IN/WRITE/DONE rows remain executed. No canonical table is
substituted for raw supply.

The carrier includes input-before-WR latches, EX blanks, incomplete banks,
descriptors, staged placements, installed/inactive code, source overwrite,
partial loans, both copy stages, receiver import, output, ACK and Ready.
Every enabled malformed input has its actual successor and receipt.
Missing tokens, busy second entry and premature unsealed reads execute
nothing. These are not typed input rejections. The positive replay theorem
uses authentic canonical code and a completed predecessor; this restriction
removes no state from the physical carrier.

